  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0164 database is a comprehensive schema that stores information about customers, products, sales, and inventory. It contains nine tables, each with its own unique purpose and structure.\nThe Customer table stores information about individual customers, including their ID, home store, first name, email, customer since date, loyalty card number, birthdate, gender, and birth year. The table also includes a primary key constraint on the customer ID column.\nThe Generation table stores information about customer generations, including the birth year and generation name.\nThe Product table stores information about products, including their ID, product group, category, type, product name, description, unit of measure, current wholesale price, current retail price, tax exempt status, promo status, and new product status. The table also includes primary key and unique constraints on the product ID column.\nThe Date table stores information about transaction dates, including the transaction date, date ID, week ID, week description, month ID, month name, quarter ID, quarter name, and year ID.\nThe Pastry Inventory table stores information about pastry inventory, including the sales outlet ID, transaction date, product ID, start of day, quantity sold, waste, and waste percentage.\nThe Sales Target table stores information about sales targets, including the sales outlet ID, year and month, beans goal, beverage goal, food goal, merchandise goal, and total goal.\nThe Sales Outlet table stores information about sales outlets, including the sales outlet ID, type, square feet, address, city, state, telephone, postal code, longitude, latitude, manager, and neighborhood. The table also includes a primary key constraint on the sales outlet ID column.\nThe Staff table stores information about staff members, including their ID, first name, last name, position, start date, and location. The table also includes a primary key constraint on the staff ID column.\nThe Sales Receipt table stores information about sales receipts, including the transaction ID, transaction date, transaction time, sales outlet ID, staff ID, customer ID, in-store status, order number, line item ID, product ID, quantity, line item amount, unit price, and promo item status. The table also includes primary key and foreign key constraints on the transaction ID, sales outlet ID, staff ID, customer ID, and product ID columns.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe coffee industry has experienced significant changes due to the COVID-19 pandemic, with reduced in-store visitors but increased demand for coffee delivery and takeaway to support people working from home. This situation necessitates a robust approach to managing operational data, specifically through implementing a data warehouse to optimize operations during various business hours.\n\n Objectives\n\n- Design a data warehouse dimensional model for analyzing operating hours in the coffee industry.\n- Enhance decision-making regarding sales, inventory, and customer engagement.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Coffee Shop Owners/Managers: Requires insights into operations, sales, and inventory.\n- Data Analysts: Utilize the data warehouse to extract meaningful insights.\n- Operational Staff: Manage sales outlets and customer engagement efficiently.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Customer Management: Maintain comprehensive customer profiles including loyalty and preferences.\n2. Product Tracking: Categorize and manage products with detailed information on pricing, promotions, and descriptions.\n3. Sales and Inventory Analysis: Track daily sales, inventory changes, waste management, and targets across outlets.\n4. Sales Outlet Management: Capture detailed outlet information including location, size, and management details.\n5. Staff Management: Maintain staff information related to roles, locations, and start dates.\n6. Transaction Handling: Record sales receipts and transaction details across outlets, capturing in-store and online sales.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support expansion to accommodate more outlets and increased data volume.\n- Security: Protect sensitive customer and financial data.\n- Data Accuracy: Ensure high data integrity and minimal errors in reporting.\n- Performance: Enable fast data retrieval and report generation even under heavy load.\n- Reliability: Maintain consistent data updates and system uptime to support seamless operations.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0164.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0164\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `home_store` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `customer_since` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `loyalty_card_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birthdate` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birth_year` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `generation` (\n  `birth_year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `generation_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`birth_year`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_group` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_of_measure` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `current_wholesale_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `current_retail_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tax_exempt` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `promo_status` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `new_product_status` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `unique_product` (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `date` (\n  `date_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `week_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `week_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `month_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `month_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quarter_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quarter_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`date_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pastry_inventory` (\n  `sales_outlet_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_of_day` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity_sold` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `waste` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `waste_percentage` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sales_outlet_id`, `transaction_date`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pastry_inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_target` (\n  `sales_outlet_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `month` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `beans_goal` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `beverage_goal` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `food_goal` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `merchandise_goal` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_goal` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sales_outlet_id`, `year`, `month`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_outlet` (\n  `sales_outlet_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `square_feet` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `telephone` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(10,8) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(10,8) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `manager` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `neighborhood` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sales_outlet_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `staff` (\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`staff_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_receipt` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `transaction_time` time DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sales_outlet_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `in_store_status` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `line_item_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `line_item_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `promo_item_status` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_receipt_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sales_outlet_id`) REFERENCES `sales_outlet` (`sales_outlet_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_receipt_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_receipt_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_receipt_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
